[A backlog outruns the capacity that held it]: Because longer waits make each case take longer, capacity that kept the list static at short waits does not at long ones, and the list keeps growing. {fidelity: "interpretation", warrant: "coherence", pinpoint: "p. 359", source: "A level of capacity that was enough to keep waiting lists static at a waiting time of 18 weeks would not be sufficient to keep waiting lists static at a waiting time of 9 months; waiting lists would continue to get longer", note: "The text closes the loop by juxtaposition: the sentence before says cases take longer as cataracts worsen and cataracts worsen as patients wait; this one says the capacity that held a short list does not hold a long one. The link from longer cases to a growing list is the text's point, not stated as a step. The author agrees with this reading (James Wilson, 30 Sep 2026).", causes: {from: casetime, to: cataractwait, sign: "+", basis: asserted, chain: cataract}}

