# Values beyond cost-effectiveness {isGroup: true}

<Humans are not photocopiers>: A machine may be run to breakdown because it is replaceable; staff may not, because overwork brings moral injury and breakdown that cannot be priced in, and neglect has instrumental costs besides. {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "p. 362"}

(1) [The photocopier may be run past its cycle]: "Machinery is replaceable: it is perfectly reasonable for an office manager to decide to allow a photocopier to be operated in excess of its monthly work cycle, in the knowledge that this will make it more likely to break down, and to require fixing by an engineer." {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 362", causes: {from: overuse, to: breakdown, sign: "+", on: chance, basis: example, design: illustration, chain: staff}}
(2) [Overwork breaks staff]
(3) [Humans not replaceable]: "Human beings are not replaceable, and a health system cannot and should not price-in the cost of staff moral injury and breakdown." {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 362", note: "Contrasted with a photocopier, which may reasonably be run past its work cycle because machinery is replaceable."}
(4) [Neglect of the human has instrumental costs]
