(1) [Prioritisation not inimical]: "Prioritisation of care is not something inimical to the goods internal to the practice of healthcare, and in some form is arguably required by such goods." {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 362"}
(2) [Rationing tension]: "the fact that care must inevitably be limited comes into tension with the responsiveness to human need and suffering that forms the ethical core of healthcare" {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 362"}
